The correct query to run in Azure Log Analytics workspace Workspace1 to view error events from the Event table is:
B. Event | where EventType == &quot;error&quot;
Why This Is Correct?
Azure Log Analytics uses Kusto Query Language (KQL).
The syntax Event | where EventType == &quot;error&quot;:
Filters the Event table
Returns only rows where the EventType column equals &quot;error&quot;
Why the Others Are Incorrect?
A. search in (Event) &quot;error&quot;
This performs a full-text search, which is less efficient and less precise than filtering with where.
C. select * from Event where EventType == &quot;error&quot;
This is SQL syntax, not valid in KQL.
D. Get-Event Event | where {$_.EventType == &quot;error&quot;}
This is PowerShell syntax, not applicable in Log Analytics queries.

